Reading: a range used as a ~90% interval should hit ~90% with median z ~0.4-0.5. Hit rate well below 90% with median z > 1 = over-confident (too narrow);
hit rate near 100% with median z << 0.5 = under-confident (too wide). Rows within one run share numbers and anchors, so they are not independent;
the Wilson intervals treat them as independent and are too narrow.

